  "method": "built-in image_gen",
  "background": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: a directly playable 2D miniature top-down game room background, one scene, 16:9 landscape.\nInput image 1 is STYLE REFERENCE only: match the top floor of this existing cyberpunk survivor safehouse exactly in camera angle, tiny detailed pixel art, scale of equipment, dark blue steel walls, slate floor tiles, cyan and magenta neon with restrained amber task lights. Generate a NEW adjacent HYDROPONICS GROW ROOM in the same safehouse after a zombie apocalypse, well maintained by survivors, not a ruin.\nLayout must be precise for game integration. Single room enclosed by walls, upper wall face occupies the top 20% of the frame, visible walkable floor spans x=3%..97%, y=25%..94%. ONLY entry/exit is an open cyan-lit rectangular doorway in the LEFT SIDE wall centered at y=59%; threshold visually connects to the clear main aisle. No other door.\nExactly THREE identical EMPTY hydroponic growing trays form one horizontal row in the upper-middle floor: centers x=30%,52%,74%, y=45%. Each tray approximately 16% canvas width and 16% canvas height, dark moist substrate and three tiny empty planting holes, a narrow cyan metal rim. NO plants growing in these three trays, because game sprites will grow dynamically over them. The tray bottom edges at y=53% leave a wide clear aisle directly below to interact.\nPerimeter details only: water filtration tank and pipe manifold against top-left wall, seed cabinets, ventilation, two greenish grow lights, survival food storage and hand tools along upper/right wall, small leafy pots on upper shelves. Restrained used patches, reused metal, warm evidence of human survival, no blood or zombies inside sanctuary. Lower half mostly empty readable tiled floor for player movement. No objects blocking the left doorway or main aisle.\nHighest polished commercially released miniature pixel game quality, crisp consistent pixel clusters, fine industrial detailing matching the reference, NOT a painting, NOT an isometric tilted diamond room, NOT 3D, not cartoon cute. No people, no characters, no HUD, no text, labels, logos or watermark. Whole room visible and uncropped. Opaque background.",
  "plants": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: TRANSPARENT game plant growth sprite atlas, 2 columns by 2 rows, four equal isolated cells with generous empty padding; 1024x1024 square.\nInput image 1 is STYLE AND SCALE REFERENCE for the same miniature pixel-art cyberpunk survivor safehouse. Create FOUR stages of the SAME edible leafy green hydroponic herb, mature commercial 2D pixel game quality, same dark outlines, crisp tiny square pixel clusters, cyan rim-light and muted emerald/olive leaves with restrained warm highlights. NOT vector art, not painted, not blurry, not kawaii.\nCell order: TOP LEFT newly planted soil with three very tiny seed sprouts; TOP RIGHT small young herb with four leaves; BOTTOM LEFT mid-grown healthy herb with eight leaves; BOTTOM RIGHT full mature harvestable herb with lush leaves and a few tiny pale-green edible buds.\nEach stage is one coherent low herb cluster, viewed from the game's high top-down 3/4 viewpoint. ALL stages share identical bottom-center root anchor and same overall scale; the mature herb canopy fits the same hydroponic tray width, no giant tree. No tray, pot, planter box, soil rectangle or background, only the living plant and a tiny natural soil/root tuft. Identical lighting in all cells. No labels, numbers, gridlines, border or text, no humans or machines. True alpha transparent background including cell gutters. This is an animation asset atlas for placing over empty game growing beds."
}
{
  "method": "built-in image_gen",
  "background": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset type: playable miniature 2D pixel-art cyberpunk survival SMART FARM interior.\nInput image 1 is the EDIT TARGET. Keep identical room footprint, camera, 16:9 canvas, wall height, left-side cyan doorway, safehouse industrial pixel-art style and equipment proportions, palette of dark navy steel/cyan/magenta/amber. Transform the primitive three soil trays into a professionally automated compact indoor smart farm. NO soil beds, individual flowerpots or troughs of dirt on the playable floor.\nDesign exactly TWELVE empty integrated hydroponic planting stations, in TWO straight horizontal banks of SIX small separate metal grow modules. Precise module centers in normalized canvas coordinates: x=24%,36%,48%,60%,72%,84%, with upper bank centers y=39%, lower bank centers y=73%. Each module width9.5% of canvas, height13%; underside includes a little plumbing and base, overhead thin LED growth bar with sensors. Flat pale mineral-wool/net-cup sockets, water circulation tubes and tiny indicator lights. Keep modules EMPTY of plants; dynamic crop sprites will be placed later. All 12 stations clear and countable, same scale. A central walkway between banks spans y=48%..62%, open from the LEFT doorway at y=55%. Perimeter walkway and lower aisle stay open too.\nMake the machinery read immediately as a controlled SMART FARM: automated nutrient dosing tank, water filtration/pump manifold, oxygenation pipes, temperature/humidity sensor boxes and an integrated small environmental computer on the top wall. Small stacked propagation shelves along top wall can suggest a vertical farm; no large obstacles in walkways. Working grow lights cool cyan with soft violet, not nightclub saturation. The sanctuary is maintained after the zombie apocalypse, subtle wear but reassuring functional life-support engineering. No people, no zombies, no robots.\nCommercially released detailed crisp pixel-game art exactly like target, no photorealism, painterly brushwork, soft 3D render or tilted isometric diamond. One finished room, not a concept collage. No HUD, headings, numbers, text or watermark. Preserve the LEFT door and its immediate aisle for movement.",
  "crops": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: real TRANSPARENT pixel-art game crop growth ATLAS for a miniature cyberpunk survivor smart farm.\nInput image 1 is STYLE REFERENCE only. Match its crisp pixel clusters, dark outlines, industrial-green plant lighting and tiny object scale, NOT cartoon vector or painted art.\nSingle tall sheet, exactly FOUR columns and SIX rows, all 24 equal cells, ample TRANSPARENT gutters. 1024x1536 portrait canvas. Each cell one isolated plant without tray, pot, dirt rectangle or infrastructure. True alpha transparent background.\nThe four columns in EVERY row are growth stages of the SAME species: 1 tiny sprouts/root crown, 2 young plant, 3 medium plant, 4 fully mature harvestable plant. Root/base anchor is bottom-center of each cell, consistent framing, no overlap between cells. Mature canopy scale stays small enough for a one-person hydroponic module.\nRows top to bottom must show SIX genuinely different silhouettes and colors:\nRow1 MEDI HERB: warm emerald medicinal broadleaf herb, small pale-yellow buds at maturity.\nRow2 SHIELD KALE: compact blue-green curly kale rosette, veined layered leaves, no metallic armor.\nRow3 ENERGY BERRY: little branching berry bush, cyan-blue clusters of edible berries at maturity.\nRow4 BLAZE PEPPER: slender dark-green pepper plant with a few clearly red-orange peppers.\nRow5 NEURO MINT: compact purple-teal mint with paired pointed leaves and small pale-lilac flower spike.\nRow6 FOCUS MUSHROOM: short edible mushroom cluster, violet caps and pale stems, smaller pin stages progressing to full cluster.\nThis is mature, polished, commercially released 2D top-down 3/4 pixel-game art, consistent perspective and light on all plants. Tiny crisp pixel blocks, muted natural hues with restrained cyan edge light. No labels, numbers, text, gridlines, outer border, humans, robots, watermarks or background. No flowerpots."
}
