  "tool": "built-in image_gen",
  "request": "Redraw every NPC to match the player sprite art style",
  "reference": "res://assets/cyberpunk/hero-sheet.png",
  "frames_per_npc": 8,
  "fps": 4,
  "game_frame_size": [
    96,
    96
  ],
  "body_height": 54,
  "prompts": [
    {
      "role": "researcher",
      "prompt": "Use case: style-transfer. Asset type: redraw an existing NPC animation sheet to match the existing PLAYER GAME SPRITE exactly. Image 1 is the PLAYER style reference and must dictate every proportion and pixel-art decision. Image 2 is the NPC identity reference ONLY, not the style. Redraw image 2 as a brand-new coherent 4-COLUMN by 2-ROW equal-cell grid containing EXACTLY EIGHT sequential idle animation frames of ONE character. Output genuine transparent RGBA, no backgrounds, no gradients, no drawn checkerboard, no text or borders. STRICT STYLE: the player in image 1 has an enormous simple rounded hair/head silhouette, oversized bright simple eyes, tiny stubby torso and legs, only about TWO HEADS TALL overall. The head including hair takes roughly 43-46 percent of total character height and is almost as wide as shoulders. Match that exact chibi low-resolution game style; simple flat readable blocks of color, dark near-black outline, only 2-3 shades per material, no fine lines, no realistic anatomy, no thin limbs, no long bodies, no painted texture, no high-detail anime illustration, no shiny rendered highlights. It should appear hand-drawn at roughly 40-50 pixels tall and then nearest-neighbor enlarged. The actual intended game sprite is 54 pixels tall, so details must remain readable at 54px. Front slightly elevated three-quarter camera looking down toward viewer exactly like player. Same identity, costume, palette, scale, facing and head size across all 8 frames. One full character per equal cell with generous gutters, body fills 65-75% of cell height. BOTH FEET planted at identical x and baseline in each cell, no walking/spinning/sliding. Eight distinct hand-drawn IDLE frames: gentle breathing, tiny prop handling gesture, eye blink, return to rest; subtle differences must remain visible after reduction to 54px. Keep the head simple and large in all frames. NO weapons or player sword. Preserve the NPC identity described below while completely replacing its old realistic/long-limbed proportions. A data researcher woman with an oversized white-silver asymmetric bob haircut and simple turquoise glasses over large bright eyes. Tiny pale off-white lab coat over a dark teal suit, short chunky boots, compact cyan handheld scanner. Idle looks at scanner, taps screen, blinks, lowers hand slightly. The coat ends above the stubby boots and does not lengthen the torso; must be TWO HEADS TALL like the PLAYER. Image 3 is an APPROVED redesigned NPC from the same cast; match its chunky large-headed silhouette, outline thickness and very simple pixel blocks so all six NPCs look like one cohesive sprite set alongside image 1. Keep your own NPC costume and identity from image 2.",
      "source": "res://assets/cyberpunk_npcs/source/researcher.png",
      "sheet": "res://assets/cyberpunk_npcs/researcher.png",
      "generated_source": "C:\\Users\\grow2\\.codex\\generated_images\\01a13ed8-e0fc-7b52-a504-62c89afbe11f\\exec-8faf645a-2b9d-4a4d-b80b-bbc85c6ef983.png"
    },
    {
      "role": "broker",
      "prompt": "Use case: style-transfer. Asset type: redraw an existing NPC animation sheet to match the existing PLAYER GAME SPRITE exactly. Image 1 is the PLAYER style reference and must dictate every proportion and pixel-art decision. Image 2 is the NPC identity reference ONLY, not the style. Redraw image 2 as a brand-new coherent 4-COLUMN by 2-ROW equal-cell grid containing EXACTLY EIGHT sequential idle animation frames of ONE character. Output genuine transparent RGBA, no backgrounds, no gradients, no drawn checkerboard, no text or borders. STRICT STYLE: the player in image 1 has an enormous simple rounded hair/head silhouette, oversized bright simple eyes, tiny stubby torso and legs, only about TWO HEADS TALL overall. The head including hair takes roughly 43-46 percent of total character height and is almost as wide as shoulders. Match that exact chibi low-resolution game style; simple flat readable blocks of color, dark near-black outline, only 2-3 shades per material, no fine lines, no realistic anatomy, no thin limbs, no long bodies, no painted texture, no high-detail anime illustration, no shiny rendered highlights. It should appear hand-drawn at roughly 40-50 pixels tall and then nearest-neighbor enlarged. The actual intended game sprite is 54 pixels tall, so details must remain readable at 54px. Front slightly elevated three-quarter camera looking down toward viewer exactly like player. Same identity, costume, palette, scale, facing and head size across all 8 frames. One full character per equal cell with generous gutters, body fills 65-75% of cell height. BOTH FEET planted at identical x and baseline in each cell, no walking/spinning/sliding. Eight distinct hand-drawn IDLE frames: gentle breathing, tiny prop handling gesture, eye blink, return to rest; subtle differences must remain visible after reduction to 54px. Keep the head simple and large in all frames. NO weapons or player sword. Preserve the NPC identity described below while completely replacing its old realistic/long-limbed proportions. A bounty broker man with an oversized head of swept-back dark purple-black hair, a broad simple magenta visor, tiny charcoal-purple short coat with magenta lapel, stubby pants and boots, compact amber tablet. Idle taps tablet, briefly touches visor with tiny hand, blinks, returns to rest. Large simple head and tiny torso exactly like PLAYER, no tall trenchcoat model or long legs. Image 3 is an APPROVED redesigned NPC from the same cast; match its chunky large-headed silhouette, outline thickness and very simple pixel blocks so all six NPCs look like one cohesive sprite set alongside image 1. Keep your own NPC costume and identity from image 2.",
      "source": "res://assets/cyberpunk_npcs/source/broker.png",
      "sheet": "res://assets/cyberpunk_npcs/broker.png",
      "generated_source": "C:\\Users\\grow2\\.codex\\generated_images\\01a13ed8-e0fc-7b52-a504-62c89afbe11f\\exec-31889716-5afd-45d8-aa03-3404bb515ea0.png"
    },
    {
      "role": "drone_tech",
      "prompt": "Use case: style-transfer. Asset type: redraw an existing NPC animation sheet to match the existing PLAYER GAME SPRITE exactly. Image 1 is the PLAYER style reference and must dictate every proportion and pixel-art decision. Image 2 is the NPC identity reference ONLY, not the style. Redraw image 2 as a brand-new coherent 4-COLUMN by 2-ROW equal-cell grid containing EXACTLY EIGHT sequential idle animation frames of ONE character. Output genuine transparent RGBA, no backgrounds, no gradients, no drawn checkerboard, no text or borders. STRICT STYLE: the player in image 1 has an enormous simple rounded hair/head silhouette, oversized bright simple eyes, tiny stubby torso and legs, only about TWO HEADS TALL overall. The head including hair takes roughly 43-46 percent of total character height and is almost as wide as shoulders. Match that exact chibi low-resolution game style; simple flat readable blocks of color, dark near-black outline, only 2-3 shades per material, no fine lines, no realistic anatomy, no thin limbs, no long bodies, no painted texture, no high-detail anime illustration, no shiny rendered highlights. It should appear hand-drawn at roughly 40-50 pixels tall and then nearest-neighbor enlarged. The actual intended game sprite is 54 pixels tall, so details must remain readable at 54px. Front slightly elevated three-quarter camera looking down toward viewer exactly like player. Same identity, costume, palette, scale, facing and head size across all 8 frames. One full character per equal cell with generous gutters, body fills 65-75% of cell height. BOTH FEET planted at identical x and baseline in each cell, no walking/spinning/sliding. Eight distinct hand-drawn IDLE frames: gentle breathing, tiny prop handling gesture, eye blink, return to rest; subtle differences must remain visible after reduction to 54px. Keep the head simple and large in all frames. NO weapons or player sword. Preserve the NPC identity described below while completely replacing its old realistic/long-limbed proportions. A drone technician woman with oversized bright cobalt-blue pixie hair/head, large orange goggles perched on top, large simple eyes, tiny burnt-orange overalls over navy sleeves, little tool belt and chunky boots. Holds a small cyan inspection drone against chest and short screwdriver. Idle adjusts drone with screwdriver, blinks, lowers tool. Keep drone small and visibly attached to hand, not a floating second character. Same TWO-HEAD-TALL simple big-headed proportions as PLAYER. Image 3 is an APPROVED redesigned NPC from the same cast; match its chunky large-headed silhouette, outline thickness and very simple pixel blocks so all six NPCs look like one cohesive sprite set alongside image 1. Keep your own NPC costume and identity from image 2.",
